@[boot-loader step]
Set up a boot loader, which starts the kernel when the machine boots. Each
choice has its own instructions:

  @[todo grub]   GRUB, on this ISO (the @[grub2] cache, installed in the
               basesystem step); works on BIOS and UEFI machines

The grimoire has others (@[limine], @[refind], @[syslinux], @[lilo]); they aren't
on this ISO, so they need network and a @[cast] in the installed system (or in
@[enchantment chroot]). The machine needs a working boot loader to start the
new system the first time, so GRUB is the simple choice now; you can switch
later.

To see these instructions again, type @[todo]. When the boot loader is set
up, type @[next] to go on to the user setup.
